  "question": {
    "text": "In a Wheatstone's network,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>. Find the resistance (in <math> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi> </math>) with which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is to be shunted, in order that the bridge gets balanced.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let a resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> be shunted with resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>, so that the bridge is balanced.<br /><br />Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">'</mo></math>&nbsp;be the resultant resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, then<br /><br />In balanced position<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/P-8.png\" style=\"width: 327px; height: 237px;\" /><br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>′</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>′</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>′</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br /><br />Now,<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>′</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>′</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
